rom May 28, 2020 to Oct 2, 2020.","setup":"The stock rose about 180% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 7 weeks, peaking at $10.93 and pulling back 32% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Aug 14, 2020 it closed at $8.06, below the base's floor of $8.67, without ever closing above the base high of $10.93. Volume that day was 3.8M shares, 7.13x the prior 10-day average. It kept sliding, down to $5.33, and the chart ends at $5.65.","lesson":"This is an example of a breakdown. The stock built what looked like a base, then broke out of the bottom instead of the top. There was never a breakout to buy. When a base gives way below, the move is to stay out, or get out fast if you bought early."}}